{"title":"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_but_quicker\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 but quicker</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Quick_Time_Trouble_Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Quick Time Trouble Solution 5</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trapezoid\" title=\"Trapezoid\">trapezoid</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> with bases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/b/49bee096a0c16c74196af6d7f047a63f31e379e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 52$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/f/d5fb59fff6b6968adfa1e4b3d06a609a2a8af375.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a346f075b2763fc03bc1e7b2bd9715e59829d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = 39$\" width=\"71\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70ca7a2802258c318f836d1bb1c82ad22bdde144.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA = 5$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/a/1fa4f0699281dfa4b8a3805dc6a50fb2c9c0e751.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D; A=(0,0); B=(52,0); C=(38,20); D=(5,20); dot(A); dot(B); dot(C); dot(D); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,S); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,S); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,N); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,N); label(&quot;52&quot;,(A+B)/2,S); label(&quot;39&quot;,(C+D)/2,N); label(&quot;12&quot;,(B+C)/2,E); label(&quot;5&quot;,(D+A)/2,W); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"135\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/0/fb026715575c692ef81c7a1017dfe063f85f49f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 182 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 195 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 210 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 234 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 260$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"421\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>It shouldn't be hard to use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trigonometry\" title=\"Trigonometry\">trigonometry</a> to bash this and find the height, but there is a much easier way. Extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> to meet at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/f/08fd9a3001f04eb9624f966ea35af9f5984fd7a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(250); defaultpen(0.8); pair A=(0,0), B = (52,0), C=(52-144/13,60/13), D=(25/13,60/13), F=(100/13,240/13); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(D--F--C,dashed); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,A,S); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,B,S); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,D,W); label(&quot;\\(E\\)&quot;,F,N); label(&quot;39&quot;,(C+D)/2,N); label(&quot;52&quot;,(A+B)/2,S); label(&quot;5&quot;,(A+D)/2,E); label(&quot;12&quot;,(B+C)/2,WSW); [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"185\" /></center>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d332902316baefe453ae84fd82954d6ada8708d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB} || \\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/a/c6a036f5ba5f0a9be15cad8a8d450cb181110c80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AEB \\sim \\triangle DEC$\" width=\"143\" height=\"13\" />, with the ratio of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Proportion\" title=\"Proportion\">proportionality</a> being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/0/ae0580575c7974f69ee16cbdadf6d40a94fabf81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {39}{52} = \\frac {3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"38\" />. Thus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/c/9ecaabe64bc78a6c0ddf43771253021e558c1778.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac {CE}{CE + 12} = \\frac {3}{4} &amp; \\Longrightarrow CE = 36 \\\\ \\frac {DE}{DE + 5} = \\frac {3}{4} &amp; \\Longrightarrow DE = 15 \\end{align*}\" width=\"219\" height=\"84\" />\nSo the sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/8/b984c55719cc5f992ee62656d920ac15c78d9137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cb8c52f3062a3269668a70a21d66ba14204e7da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15,36,39$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" />, which we recognize to be a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/0/e80dfc0a2f09378b7e077614d426bef327aee8f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 - 12 - 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"89\" height=\"13\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_triangle\" title=\"Right triangle\">right triangle</a>. Therefore (we could simplify some of the calculation using that the ratio of areas is equal to the ratio of the sides squared),\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac44872ef92e9370f6abc0ca1ef24d5881ef346e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABCD] = [ABE] - [CDE] = \\frac {1}{2}\\cdot 20 \\cdot 48 - \\frac {1}{2} \\cdot 15 \\cdot 36 = \\boxed{\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 210}\\]\" width=\"514\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Draw altitudes from points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/255b3ee5b7acb3f4baca3b52720811aa66cba79e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.2cm); defaultpen(0.8); pair A=(0,0), B = (52,0), C=(52-144/13,60/13), D=(25/13,60/13), E=(52-144/13,0), F=(25/13,0); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(C--E,dashed); draw(D--F,dashed); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,A,SW); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,B,S); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,D,N); label(&quot;\\(D&#39;\\)&quot;,F,SSE); label(&quot;\\(C&#39;\\)&quot;,E,S); label(&quot;39&quot;,(C+D)/2,N); label(&quot;52&quot;,(A+B)/2,S); label(&quot;5&quot;,(A+D)/2,W); label(&quot;12&quot;,(B+C)/2,ENE); [/asy]\" width=\"525\" height=\"92\" /></center>\n<p>Translate the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/a/27a4835d23f08f296a98865dc7255b7d03655689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADD&#39;$\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/5/825000b887cf170e8a54ee5dcdafffbdfb959cea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DD&#39;$\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> coincides with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44b7058f8a28ca225136b284b337138a54e39e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CC&#39;$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. We get the following triangle:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae9e06d7e09ef1c45cb1eb1354f20938e46480b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.2cm); defaultpen(0.8); pair A=(0,0), B = (13,0), C=(25/13,60/13), F=(25/13,0); draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(C--F,dashed); label(&quot;\\(A&#39;\\)&quot;,A,SW); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,B,S); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,C,N); label(&quot;\\(C&#39;\\)&quot;,F,SE); label(&quot;5&quot;,(A+C)/2,W); label(&quot;12&quot;,(B+C)/2,ENE); [/asy]\" width=\"162\" height=\"88\" /></center>\n<p>The length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/c/22cf0fa25e560981109abb13757436b94fadb035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> in this triangle is equal to the length of the original <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, minus the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />.\nThus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/e/2fe4b9e43fa4e12ce6a617b42cb57d97efd4dbef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B = 52 - 39 = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"157\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4b7c6fecba4010b78b71bed438ac506d39587f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;BC$\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> is a well-known <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/0/a604be7f74f466e9c452dab1a5fd92e5da74bddf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5,12,13)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" /> right triangle. Its area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/3/54322280d1b10baf6ca8edd14c369866e1f35e0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[A&#39;BC]=\\frac{A&#39;C\\cdot BC}2 = \\frac{5\\cdot 12}2 = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"270\" height=\"38\" />, and therefore its altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44b7058f8a28ca225136b284b337138a54e39e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CC&#39;$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/e/94e8a9c6a0cc4556e0cf07f422717e08d1688865.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[A&#39;BC]}{A&#39;B} = \\frac{60}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>Now the area of the original trapezoid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/a/0ca93e61f77442f741da5cf26a0cbd4c5eb86c7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(AB+CD)\\cdot CC&#39;}2 = \\frac{91 \\cdot 60}{13 \\cdot 2} = 7\\cdot 30 = \\boxed{\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 210}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"383\" height=\"39\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Draw altitudes from points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/255b3ee5b7acb3f4baca3b52720811aa66cba79e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.2cm); defaultpen(0.8); pair A=(0,0), B = (52,0), C=(52-144/13,60/13), D=(25/13,60/13), E=(52-144/13,0), F=(25/13,0); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(C--E,dashed); draw(D--F,dashed); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,A,SW); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,B,S); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,D,N); label(&quot;\\(D&#39;\\)&quot;,F,SSE); label(&quot;\\(C&#39;\\)&quot;,E,S); label(&quot;39&quot;,(C+D)/2,N); label(&quot;52&quot;,(A+B)/2,S); label(&quot;5&quot;,(A+D)/2,W); label(&quot;12&quot;,(B+C)/2,ENE); [/asy]\" width=\"525\" height=\"92\" /></center>\n<p>Call the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/8/ad8019d0fb176ff1ade21d8a9e6d6aa4a1f9563a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/c/5bc856e7f29652b2c928f2c025ed9befbab1873e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC&#39;$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and the height of the trapezoid to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\nBy the Pythagorean Theorem, we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/5/8a5e174f37eebd2336bbcabec233ee1e1bdf2561.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z^2 + x^2 = 144\\]\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a04142ba36ef09072723ba5c0ec7e840f3ba2ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y^2 + x^2 = 25\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting these two equation yields:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/7/3570d2493e77ace9a387502ad4d1a0a9d354a56f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z^2-y^2=119 \\implies (z+y)(z-y)=119\\]\" width=\"317\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>We also have: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d4251004edb6d9284503170c0cce3d98b16b01d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z+y=52-39=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"165\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>We can substitute the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/5/955b0030c06d258b4b9a46188afd9c88bb91634c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> into the equation we just obtained, so we now have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/2/1b2ea34d8c8f15fc45d7d39c6286cfdb62f58185.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(13) (z-y)=119 \\implies z-y=\\frac{119}{13}\\]\" width=\"281\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>We can add the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/5/955b0030c06d258b4b9a46188afd9c88bb91634c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/1/3f1d516db531c1a66f4f54fec76743404a5c06b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"11\" /> equation to find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, which simplifies down to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e11daf15318eb2664a432383c49e19f02a61268.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{144}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" />. Finally, we can plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and use the Pythagorean theorem to find the height of the trapezoid.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4bcff5389251371e3013c9914d75d23521f3121.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{12^4}{13^2} + x^2 = 12^2 \\implies x^2 = \\frac{(12^2)(13^2)}{13^2} -\\frac{12^4}{13^2}  \\implies x^2 = \\frac{(12 \\cdot 13)^2 - (144)^2}{13^2} \\implies x^2 = \\frac{(156+144)(156-144)}{13^2} \\implies x = \\sqrt{\\frac{3600}{169}} = \\frac{60}{13}\\]\" width=\"1030\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Now that we have the height of the trapezoid, we can multiply this by the median to find our answer.\n</p><p>The median of the trapezoid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/2/fc2a67c74b75fa1b00861f857e738ca400b59e48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{39+52}{2} = \\frac{91}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"107\" height=\"37\" />, and multiplying this and the height of the trapezoid gets us:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/0/5200e426505fe8439347aa5bdea83897e4c818b5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{60 \\cdot 91}{13 \\cdot 2} = \\boxed{\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 210}\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We construct a line segment parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f694ab8315c055ae7dd5d9fe5ba57a1a7c97a99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"19\" /> and label the intersection of this segment with line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> as point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/710fb5fa3adedd7a16739e543d846747adbe05b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> Then quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/421b4b2fbd1b67330bf1605c6901f73fcefdb5e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AECD$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> is a parallelogram, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/5/a15bb4d09ad85730d936e67ce079180bb315d095.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE=5, AE=39,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc46235a1bd1364f27a04fff1d1a68bbfb610f33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EB=13.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" /> Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/27282aafa81e06b3343e93b3e9221570c0d14be2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EBC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is therefore a right triangle, with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a65ac81561b3113532ab571e47ff4dd6579c058b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac12 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 12 = 30.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>By continuing to split <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> into segments of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf16d3a16d64a9f26214054355b52da40acce300.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" /> we can connect these vertices in a \"zig-zag,\" creating seven congruent right triangles, each with sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/2/dc24a7d9b78eaaa38a1bcea8ba1e2baafe0643c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5,12,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf16d3a16d64a9f26214054355b52da40acce300.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" /> and each with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2a8c6bab62d0931b9d43a9658b409b14b8d7c03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30.$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" /> The total area is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/c/3ec2d4aca560193bb39fcc95bd5208f48a885cf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\cdot 30 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} 210}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"135\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>Alternative: Instead of creating seven congruent right triangles, we can find the height of parallelogram <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/421b4b2fbd1b67330bf1605c6901f73fcefdb5e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AECD$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> by drawing an altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, creating the new point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. By recognizing that triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/b/31b0f04577d6b6bf91efc86f609edb160cfadb1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DAF$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> is similar to triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef14ba8fc495f2a5750a5ed394ebf75a28641658.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BEC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, we can use properties of similar triangles and find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/a/84aca09a3514adcffa8b19e6038f95106cf6cd10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = 12 \\cdot \\frac{5}{13} = \\frac{60}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"156\" height=\"38\" />. Thus, the area of parallelogram <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/421b4b2fbd1b67330bf1605c6901f73fcefdb5e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AECD$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f15e15d6f209619b1470ffc8f9a4bff31c3716b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{60}{13} \\cdot 39 = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"38\" />. Finally, we add the areas of the parallelogram <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/421b4b2fbd1b67330bf1605c6901f73fcefdb5e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AECD$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> and the right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef14ba8fc495f2a5750a5ed394ebf75a28641658.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BEC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> together and we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31a8f0166eea34a43e8f0bef07aa6af52735f0f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180 + 30 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} 210}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"161\" height=\"30\" />. ~scarletsyc\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_but_quicker\">Solution 2 but quicker</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 but quicker\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>From Solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> we know that the the altitude of the trapezoid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/c/7ac94a5f6297a7d6aadbd7ba04e3a0a732298908.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{60}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> and the triangle's area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\nNote that once we remove the triangle we get a rectangle with length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e058d401a1b942f106f081ff1fcca8a8b1d42a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/c/7ac94a5f6297a7d6aadbd7ba04e3a0a732298908.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{60}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />.\nThe numbers multiply nicely to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/8/fe8fd8be56d3d23a1dc218eab655776c33bbccf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180+30=\\boxed{(C) 210}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"159\" height=\"29\" />\n-harsha12345\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Quick_Time_Trouble_Solution_5\">Quick Time Trouble Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Quick Time Trouble Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>First note how the answer choices are all integers.\nThe area of the trapezoid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fb1f4e1beea2804334b2127c3c9b87136201f46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{39+52}{2} \\cdot h = \\frac{91}{2} h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"145\" height=\"38\" />. So h divides 2. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/3/7d3914c5607bf46949390af4e088bb17107565ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2h$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. The area is now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/4/7b4dc067f9e632f3b0ec28842c84cc2f4835a6e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />. \nTrying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> can easily be seen to not work. Those make the only integers possible so now you know x is a fraction. \nSince the area is an integer the denominator of x must divide either 13 or 7 since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/f/23fbf360a9dd912ce80418e843a4776dc54c34b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91 = 13\\cdot7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />.\nSeeing how <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b92c9b345408bdbab1e4ec0521e9de78392bb1ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39 = 3\\cdot13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/1/c9189b05f41461a0636221a68837c3293f27ddd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52 = 4\\cdot13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" /> assume that the denominator divides 13. Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/f/23f5acd61732085d1301940ab83e05fbf4f79d8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{x}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"54\" height=\"33\" /> the area is now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af0fd07926b28ae4ff8b90a9f1487344e977067c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />.\nNote that (A) and (C) are the only multiples of 7. We know that A doesn't work because that would mean <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> which we ruled out. \nSo the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e016c30aa0726100db6221fe483fff310c1e24f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} 210}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"67\" height=\"28\" />. - megateleportingrobots\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A\">2002 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>-(Last question)</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index